meta {
  name: Send Message
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/communications/send
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "channel": "SMS",
    "feature": "lab_order_report_published_inform_patient",
    "recipients": [
      { "recipientType": "PATIENT", "recipientName": "Rohan Mehta", "toAddress": "+919999999999" }
    ],
    "variables": { "test_name": "CBC", "report_link": "https://portal.example.com/r/abc" },
    "campaign": "August Reports"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (Array.isArray(data) && data[0] && data[0].id) bru.setEnvVar("communicationId", data[0].id);
}

docs {
  Compose + queue a message (Email / SMS / WhatsApp) to one or more recipients.
  Tenant + active branch come from the JWT — never the body (CLAUDE.md §4.7).

  The body is resolved in this precedence:
    1. explicit `body` (free text),
    2. `templateId` (a Template in the caller's scope),
    3. `feature` → the best active template for that feature + channel
       (branch → tenant → SITE_ADMIN global fallback).

  Placeholders (`{pn}`, `{patient_name}`, `{test_name}`, …) are substituted from
  `variables` (plus each recipient's name). One PENDING `communication_logs` row
  is created per recipient; the background worker delivers via the Exchange
  gateway. Captures the first row id as `communicationId`.

  ## Fields
  - `channel` (required): `EMAIL` | `SMS` | `WHATSAPP` (in-app uses /notifications).
  - `templateId` / `feature` / `body`: at least one required (see precedence).
  - `subject`: email subject (ignored for SMS/WhatsApp).
  - `recipients[]` (required, ≥1): `{ recipientType, recipientId?, recipientName?, toAddress }`.
  - `variables`: placeholder map (keys WITHOUT braces).
  - `attachments[]`: `{ data (base64), name, type }`.
  - `schedule` / `expiryDate`: ISO datetimes (defer / drop-after).
  - `campaign`, `userTimezone`: optional.
}
